InstructCell model architecture
Pre-trained LM
The architecture of pretrained language models (PLMs) can be categorized as encoder-only [62, 63, 64, 65], decoderonly [66, 67, 68, 3], or encoder-decoder [69, 24, 70, 71]. Since the three single-cell tasks considered in this study can all be formulated as sequence-to-sequence (seq2seq) tasks, any decoder-only or encoder-decoder PLM can flexibly serve as the backbone network of InstructCell . To simplify the notation in mathematical formulations, we denote the backbone network's forward computation process (excluding the transformation of input sequences into input embeddings) as p PLM ( · ; θ ).
Single-cell understanding task For the single-cell understanding task, given an input sequence X and the corresponding target sequence Y = ( y 1 , y 2 , · · · , y L target ), where y i is the i -th token in the target sequence, the objective of LM is to minimize the negative log joint probability of the target sequence [62]:
