Task definition. Task T6 focuses on chromosome-level classification of DNA sequences and serves as a non-grounding baseline task. Given one or multiple rendered DNA pages corresponding to a single DNA sequence, the model is required to predict which human chromosome the sequence originates from. Unlike Tasks T1-T5, Task T6 does not involve spatial grounding, region localization, or bounding box reasoning. Instead, it evaluates the model's ability to aggregate global sequence-level information from a visual DNA representation and perform high-level semantic classification.
